    "narrative": "Our strongest plays for today\u2019s slate are anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (80.87) and **Brice Turang** (68.83). **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Roki Sasaki; while the SP\u2019s talent is notable, the \"Slow SP Delivery\" variable provides a critical +4% boost to our SB probability, which we are weighting heavily today. Similarly, **Brice Turang** is a must-start at UTIL due to his lead-off spot against Zebby Matthews and the same base-stealing environmental advantage. **Mickey Moniak** (68.23) rounds out our elite tier, as he draws a significant +14% platoon advantage against Kyle Leahy, effectively neutralizing his poor park factor. While **Gabriel Moreno** (60.51) and **Isaac Paredes** (59.92) reside on the border of our strong tier, both are locked in due to expected #3 spots in their respective lineups, which provide the counting stat security required to chase Roto points.\n\nThe bench decision that caused the most internal debate was the exclusion of **Josh Naylor** (47.41). He was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his upside was severely suppressed by the matchup against Drew Rasmussen. The optimizer favored the floor provided by **Max Muncy** (52.48) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (53.01) due to park and platoon factors, despite Rasmussen's fading xERA. We are also monitoring a 38% rain risk for **Jose Caballero** (50.70) and **Austin Riley** (50.15). While their raw projections remain above our bench threshold, their late-order placement (Assumed #8) makes them prime candidates to be swapped out if lineups confirm they are hitting at the bottom of the order and weather reports worsen. Note that **James Wood** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving no chance for a bench injection should conditions shift for our lower-tier starters.",
